    "created_at": "2017-02-03T06:58:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-03T07:00:39Z",
    "body": "To really boil it down, I think it might be helpful to say something to the effect of \"if using a conventional '+'-separated URL scheme, the last segment is what matters to the network location\". Nip the ordering spat in the bud while everyone still agrees. (As another example, I believe docker uses `http+unix://` to refer to http over unix domain socket) (they should probably be using the `file` scheme)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
