    "created_at": "2017-02-09T10:26:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-09T10:29:09Z",
    "body": "@annevk I understand your desire not to complicate the parser even more. The most I can hope for is someone to make a small note of the plus-convention for delineating multiple protocols/schemes. But to be clear, you can't \"just use `//`\". Whether or not a URL can have a `//` is defined on a per-scheme basis. `file:///x/y/z` is valid, whereas `mailto://x@y.z` is not.\r\n\r\nThere are dozens of schemes registered already, and with the + convention, there are dozens more that will likely bypass registration. A sensible heuristic isn't the worst thing to document.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
