    "body": "Good read!\r\n\r\nI suspect that to properly standardize this \"+\" scheme convention you'd have to go for [RFC8615](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8615) and generate a ton of URI scheme drafts for IANA for all possible combinations which will in high likelihood be rejected by \"the experts\" (as noted in the aforementioned RFC)?:\r\n\r\nhttps://www.iana.org/assignments/uri-schemes/uri-schemes.xhtml\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_URI_schemes\r\n\r\nPointing this out since I've been doing some [research on this topic for work](https://github.com/samtools/hts-specs/issues/581). \r\n\r\nPlease let me know if I'm wrong with my assumption(s).",
